<heading>go - Move to another box.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
go DIRECTION
go NAME
go ..
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Moves to a connected box via a connection or to a child box. The target is
matched by endpoint name first, then by orientation (compass word or
angle, relative to the room you stand in).
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
Use go .. to move back to the parent box. Following a connection that
leads into another world moves you into that world.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
go 90
  Follow the endpoint at 90° from where you stand.

go Kitchen
  Move to a box or endpoint called Kitchen.

go ..
  Move back to the parent box.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
dig, enter, leave, look, refine split
</paragraph>
